extends layout.pug

block content-header
  link(rel='stylesheet', type='text/css', href='/style/team.css')

block content-block
  .page-content
    h1 About
    p GNIS-LD is the Linked Data version of the <a href="https://www.usgs.gov/tools/geographic-names-information-system-gnis" target="_blank">Geographic Names Information System</a>, the U.S. federal gazetteer maintained by the USGS and the Board on Geographic Names. It gives every named feature (more than two million summits, streams, lakes, and populated places) a permanent, dereferenceable URI, and makes the full record queryable over SPARQL and downloadable as quarterly versioned releases.
    p The service exists so that anyone can anchor their data to stable, authoritative geographic identifiers instead of ambiguous place-name strings.

    h2 Open Source Governance
    .steward-row
      a.steward-logo(href='https://www.dataone.org/' target='_blank' aria-label='DataONE')
        img(src='/images/dataone.svg' alt='DataONE logo')
      p.steward-text GNIS-LD is an open-source project stewarded by <a href="https://www.dataone.org/" target="_blank">DataONE</a>, whose mission is making earth and environmental data open, persistent, and accessible. As steward, DataONE operates the infrastructure, maintains the software, and is accountable for the service's availability and the dataset's integrity.
    h2 Emeritus Team
    p The project was created at the <a href="https://www.geog.ucsb.edu/services/research-facilities" target="_blank">UCSB STKO Lab</a> and later maintained under the KnowWhereGraph project, funded by NSF grant <a href="https://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/showAward?AWD_ID=2033521" target="_blank">#2033521</a>; the grant has since concluded, and stewardship passed to DataONE. The original team, from the UCSB STKO Lab and USGS:
